{:edb/db-before-t 1549 :edb/db-after-t 1550 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534862 50 #inst "2026-10-08T09:24:46.011Z" 13194139534862 true] [17592186078347 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315671 13194139534862 true] [17592186078347 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315681 13194139534862 true] [17592186078349 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315678 13194139534862 true] [17592186078888 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534862 true] [17592186078888 1100 "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\int }_{6}^{3}\\frac{1}{5}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139534862 true] [17592186078888 1100 "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that $∫_{6}^{3}\\frac{1}{5}f(x)dx =-1$ and $∫_{0}^{3}f(x)dx = 3$. What is the value of $∫_{0}^{6}f(x)dx$?" 13194139534862 false] [17592186078888 1145 "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{6}^{3}\\frac{1}{5}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{6}^{3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ {\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3+5 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315671 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315672 13194139534862 true] [17592186315671 1089 "q-114019" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315671 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534862 true] [17592186315671 1100 "Given that ${\\int }_{1}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1,$ calculate\n${\\int }_{-1}^{1}(f(x)-6x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315671 1113 #uuid "6209eb05-365f-5911-a012-6087af30a3b6" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315671 1145 "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{1}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(f(x)-6x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-6{\\int }_{-1}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =1-3({1}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =1-3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315673 13194139534862 true] [17592186315672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315674 13194139534862 true] [17592186315672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315675 13194139534862 true] [17592186315672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315676 13194139534862 true] [17592186315672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315677 13194139534862 true] [17592186315672 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534862 true] [17592186315672 1041 "selection" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315672 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315673 13194139534862 true] [17592186315672 1110 #uuid "df61f736-c1c7-51db-8e7d-78faa3e261ff" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315673 1034 "1" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534862 true] [17592186315673 1111 #uuid "49f705ac-2a39-58af-91cf-eaba9be5a7ba" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315674 1034 "-4" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315674 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534862 true] [17592186315674 1111 #uuid "f6cbd999-b9e5-524a-a637-85186fc69ddf" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315675 1034 "0" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315675 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534862 true] [17592186315675 1111 #uuid "34a0c263-cabf-54f3-8a79-523f1042ebba" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315676 1034 "-1" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315676 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534862 true] [17592186315676 1111 #uuid "92291d58-9c29-5d69-b30b-4b37071a27ed" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315677 1034 "5" 13194139534862 true] [17592186315677 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534862 true] [17592186315677 1111 #uuid "e4b1a8a7-9944-5870-8e81-7e80620cabba" 131941395